    'news.item.bytes.title': 'One token is only 7 bytes',
    'news.item.bytes.body': '1 opcode byte + 3 bytes of input A + 3 bytes of input B. Tiny on-chain records make logic-as-data practical.',
    'news.item.token.title': 'Transistors are ERC-1155 tokens',
    'news.item.token.body': 'Fungible tokens: one token is one NAND gate, minted, burned and transferred through the standard interface.',
    'news.item.nft.title': 'Circuits are ERC-721 NFTs',
    'news.item.nft.body': 'After tape-out the circuit becomes an NFT with its netlist, pin count and 7-byte gate records on chain.',
    'news.item.eval.title': 'eval is a read-only call',
    'news.item.eval.body': 'No wallet, no transaction, no gas; a hostile circuit can at worst return a wrong answer.',
    'news.item.clock.title': 'Blocks are the clock',
    'news.item.clock.body': 'BNB Chain produces a block about every 0.45 s → 2.22 Hz; the on-chain CPU advances one cycle per block.',
    'news.item.sizes.title': 'Remember 5 / 9 / 36',
    'news.item.sizes.body': 'Half adder 5 gates, full adder 9, 4-bit adder 36 — the most useful scale references in the protocol.',
    'news.item.lego.title': 'Taped-out circuits are LEGO bricks',
    'news.item.lego.body': 'Drop a half adder into a new canvas as a black box; reuse is simple but grows 9 gates to 13.',
    'news.item.behemoth.title': 'Behemoth: a 2300-transistor on-chain CPU',
    'news.item.behemoth.body': 'A 4-bit processor modelled on the 4004; it keeps running as long as the chain does.',
    'news.item.rover.title': 'TapeRover safety gate',
    'news.item.rover.body': '16 inputs, 80 NAND gates, 4 mutually exclusive outputs; all 65,536 input rows audited.',
    'news.item.hardware.title': 'From the browser to a breadboard',
    'news.item.hardware.body': 'The hardware tab translates a netlist into 74HC00 count, pin assignment, BOM and wiring list.',
    'news.item.sevenseg.title': 'Seven-segment: protocol 100, implementation 110',
    'news.item.sevenseg.body': 'The protocol describes ~100 transistors; the synthesizer actually emits 110 NAND gates, and the UI shows the real count.',
    'news.item.safety.title': 'Why mutual-exclusion audits matter',
    'news.item.safety.body': 'A safety circuit must have exactly one true output for every input; exhaustive audit is the most direct proof.',
